  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the comparative racial stereotype presented in the meme",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the meme's overall intent, which frames the viewer as someone who understands and internalizes the racialized comparison being made between 'white people after 10 shots' and 'black people after 10 shots'. The user is not explicitly directed to a specific visual or textual element with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the entire meme structure invites the user to adopt the perspective of the stereotype being presented — viewing the top image as 'wild' and the bottom as 'composed' — thereby projecting themselves into the interpretive framework of the meme's racial hierarchy. The projection is onto the conceptual scene and textual material that together construct the harmful stereotype.",
